<title>USA: SGV Bancorp to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>SGV Bancorp to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>WEST COVINA, Calif. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>SGV Bancorp Inc said it received regulatory clearance to buy back up to 10 percent, or 259,127, of its outstanding common stock.</p>
<p>The purchases will be made from time to time in open-market transactions, subject to the availability of stock. The company said it completed a repurchase of 136,380 shares in March.</p>
<p>SGV Bancorp is the holding company for First Federal Savings and Loan Association of San Gabriel Valley in West Covina, California.</p>
